(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[8 1 "// Descriptors (PY5c; CPython's Objects/descrobject.c, funcobject.c's classmethod and staticmethod,"] [9 1 "// classobject.c's method, typeobject.c's super and slot wrappers): bound methods, functions as"] [10 1 "// descriptors, classmethod, staticmethod, property, __slots__' members, super, the slot wrappers"] [11 1 "// that show a built-in type's slots as methods, and the attributes of types, functions and methods."] [15 2 "// MethodWrapperType is method-wrapper (descrobject.c's _PyMethodWrapper_Type, queue 290): a slot wrapper bound to an"] [16 2 "// instance ((2).__pow__, object().__str__), a *Method whose Func is a *slotWrapper; inspect's _NonUserDefinedCallables"] [17 2 "// tell it from a Python bound method"] [19 2 "// ClassMethodDescrType is classmethod_descriptor (descrobject.c's PyClassMethodDescr_Type, queue 290): a built-in"] [20 2 "// type's class method as its class holds it (dict.__dict__['fromkeys']), a *ClassMethod not made by classmethod()"] [21 2 "// around a *Builtin"] [32 1 "// Method is a bound method: a function and the object it is bound to."] [44 1 "// ClassMethod and StaticMethod wrap a callable."] [46 12 "// made by classmethod(...), not a built-in type's"] [58 1 "// isDescr: c is a built-in type's classmethod_descriptor (a *Builtin not wrapped by classmethod())."] [74 1 "// Property is property(fget, fset, fdel, doc)."] [78 27 "// a subclass of property"] [88 1 "// Member is a __slots__ entry's descriptor."] [97 1 "// Super is super(type, obj)."] [106 1 "// slotWrapper is a built-in type's slot as a method (wrapper_descriptor)."] [115 1 "// mappingProxy is a type's __dict__ read only."] [118 11 "// the type whose __dict__ it is, or nil"] [119 11 "// the mapping, when it is no dict (mappingproxy(UserDict()))"] [122 1 "// proxied is the mapping behind p: a built-in type's __dict__ is its dict with the getsets and the own slots' wrappers"] [123 1 "// its subscript finds (ownSlot), as one dict (builtinTypeDict; queue 313, review 307's finding 3: keys, items, len and"] [124 1 "// iteration missed int's real and every slot wrapper, which in, [] and .get found)"] [135 1 "// slotdefOrder: the slots' names in typeobject.c's slotdefs order (add_operators fills a static type's dict so),"] [136 1 "// __new__ first (its tp_new wrapper goes in before them)"] [148 1 "// builtinTypeDicts: each built-in type's merged __dict__, kept while its dict and the types' epoch stand"] [157 1 "// builtinTypeDict is t's __dict__ as CPython's type_ready_fill_dict fills it: the own slots' wrappers (add_operators),"] [158 1 "// then the dict's entries (pyi's methods, in their order), then the getsets and members (type_add_members,"] [159 1 "// type_add_getset) in their declaration order, then __doc__ (type_dict_set_doc); a name the dict has is the dict's"] [203 28 "// type_dict_set_doc, last"] [225 1 "// newWrappers are the built-in types' __new__ objects, one each."] [233 1 "// slotWrappers keep one wrapper per type and name, so that int.__repr__ is int.__repr__ (enum compares"] [234 1 "// a class's methods with its data type's and object's; PY5e, part 2b)."] [237 1 "// slotWrapperFor is built-in type m's slot for the special method name, or nil."] [245 3 "// METH_COEXIST (queue 290): the method its type defines beside the slot, a method_descriptor"] [246 3 "// (frozenset.__contains__ bound is a builtin_function_or_method: keyword.iskeyword)"] [247 3 "// objectDescr: bound to the instance itself, as the slot wrapper was (a dict subclass's __missing__:"] [248 3 "// urllib.parse's _Quoter(dict).__getitem__)"] [257 1 "// coexistMethods are the built-in types' METH_COEXIST methods (dict_methods', list_methods', set_methods' and"] [258 1 "// frozenset_methods' __getitem__ and __contains__): method descriptors where the other slots have slot wrappers."] [278 5 "// object's own slots take the instance itself, not a built-in subclass's value: object.__str__ of an"] [279 5 "// int subclass is re